1. Covered material and product scope

This license applies only to the original copyrightable material that LKVexa owns or is authorized to license in the repository identified above (the "Preview Material"). It includes the VIVIAN LCTL Reciprocal Agent source identified by the basename player_reciprocal.lctlc, its corresponding .brir and .brimg policy artifacts, and the accompanying original runner, integration examples, tests, configuration, and documentation, to the extent present. Separately licensed third-party material is excluded, as explained in section 2. This license does not grant rights in other VIVIAN agent repositories or the VIVIAN application itself.

The Reciprocal Agent copies the opponent's previous observed action, using action 0 as its opening input. Its preview scope includes evaluating that response-to-history policy within the VIVIAN game stage. The policy neither observes the opponent's current simultaneous move nor guarantees cooperation or a stable outcome.

The .brimg artifacts in this repository are compiled executable policies, not trained neural-model weights. No BRIM language-model weights, model checkpoints, tokenizer assets, or training datasets are supplied or licensed by this license. References to future model integration do not grant rights in a model; any model obtained separately remains subject to its own terms.

